<title>FRANCE: Unseasonal fire hits southern France forest.</title>
<headline>Unseasonal fire hits southern France forest.</headline>
<dateline>BORDEAUX, France 1997-04-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Firemen backed by aircraft on Saturday battled a forest fire which destroyed 500 hectares (1,250 acres) of pines near the southwestern French town of Bordeaux.</p>
<p>Firemen said no-one was injured. The blaze was out of control but was not threatening any home.</p>
<p>Drought and unseasonally high temperatures have raised fears of forest fires across southern France.</p>
</text>
